<% content_for :title, "Code of Conduct" %>
<% content_for :description, "B'more on Rails' anti-harassment policy, what we expect from each other, and how to report a problem." %>

<%#
  The blockquoted policy below is the group's ADOPTED text, reproduced
  verbatim from github.com/bmoreonrails/meetup. It is quoted in every Luma
  event listing, so it is the version people have already agreed to.

  Do not edit it here. If the policy should change, change it in that repo
  and copy the new text across — otherwise the site and the canonical
  document drift apart and nobody knows which one governs.

  Everything outside the quote is site guidance: how the policy is put into
  practice. That is ours to write. Two things still need an organizer:
  the reporting address in app/models/site.rb, and whether to name the
  organizers who handle reports.
%>

<article class="bg-white">
  <header class="bg-harbor-900 px-4 py-12 sm:px-6 sm:py-16">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <h1 class="font-display text-4xl font-bold text-marble-50 sm:text-5xl">
        Code of Conduct
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-harbor-100">
        B'more on Rails is meant to be one of the friendlier rooms you can walk
        into. Our anti-harassment policy is what we hold each other to, and it
        applies to everyone: attendees, speakers, sponsors, and organizers.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6 sm:py-16">
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-12">
      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold text-harbor-900 sm:text-3xl">
          Our anti-harassment policy
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-harbor-700">
          This is the policy the group has adopted, reproduced in full.
        </p>

        <blockquote class="mt-5 border-l-4 border-brick-500 bg-marble-50 py-6 pr-6 pl-6 sm:pl-8">
          <div class="flex flex-col gap-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-harbor-800">
            <p>
              B'more on Rails is dedicated to providing a harassment-free meetup
              experience for everyone, regardless of gender, sexual orientation,
              disability, physical appearance, body size, race, or religion. We
              do not tolerate harassment of meetup participants in any form.
              Sexual language and imagery is not appropriate for any B'more on
              Rails venue, including talks. Meetup participants violating these
              rules may be sanctioned or expelled from B'more on Rails at the
              discretion of the meetup organizers.
            </p>
            <p>
              Harassment includes offensive verbal comments related to gender,
              sexual orientation, disability, physical appearance, body size,
              race, religion, sexual images in public spaces, deliberate
              intimidation, stalking, following, harassing photography or
              recording, sustained disruption of talks or other events,
              inappropriate physical contact, and unwelcome sexual attention.
              Participants asked to stop any harassing behavior are expected to
              comply immediately.
            </p>
            <p>
              If a participant engages in harassing behavior, the meetup
              organizers may take any action they deem appropriate, including
              warning the offender or expulsion from the meetup. If you are
              being harassed, notice that someone else is being harassed, or
              have any other concerns, please contact a member of meetup
              organizers immediately.
            </p>
            <p>
              Meetup organizers will be happy to help participants contact venue
              security or local law enforcement, provide escorts, or otherwise
              assist those experiencing harassment to feel safe for the duration
              of the meetup. We value your attendance.
            </p>
          </div>
        </blockquote>

        <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-harbor-600">
          Adapted from the
          <%= link_to "Geek Feminism conference anti-harassment policy", Site::POLICY_SOURCE_URL,
                target: "_blank", rel: "noopener",
                class: "rounded-sm underline decoration-harbor-300 underline-offset-4 transition hover:text-harbor-900 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-harbor-500" %>.
          The canonical copy lives in
          <%= link_to "our meetup repository", Site::POLICY_URL,
                target: "_blank", rel: "noopener",
                class: "rounded-sm underline decoration-harbor-300 underline-offset-4 transition hover:text-harbor-900 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-harbor-500" %>;
          if the two ever disagree, that one governs.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="rounded-xl border-2 border-brick-200 bg-brick-50 p-6 sm:p-8">
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold text-harbor-900 sm:text-3xl">
          Reporting a problem
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-harbor-800">
          Tell an organizer. At an event, organizers introduce themselves at the
          start of the night and are the people to find — and as the policy
          says, they will help you contact venue security or law enforcement,
          walk you to your car, or do whatever else you need to feel safe. You
          can also write to us:
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4">
          <%= link_to Site::CONDUCT_EMAIL, "mailto:#{Site::CONDUCT_EMAIL}",
                class: "rounded-sm font-display text-lg font-semibold break-all text-brick-700 underline decoration-brick-300 underline-offset-4 transition hover:text-brick-900 hover:decoration-brick-700 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-brick-500 sm:text-xl" %>
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-harbor-800">
          You don't need to be certain, and you don't need to have been the
          person it happened to. "This felt off and I wanted someone to know" is
          a complete report.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-harbor-800">
          Reports are handled confidentially. We will not share your name with
          the person you're reporting without your agreement, and we will not
          ask you to repeat the story to a room full of people. You are welcome
          to bring someone with you when you talk to us.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold text-harbor-900 sm:text-3xl">
          How we read this policy
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-harbor-800">
          The policy lists the characteristics it protects. We read that list as
          a floor, not a ceiling. Harassment on the basis of gender identity or
          expression, neurotype, age, national origin, or how long someone has
          been writing code is harassment, and it gets the same response.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-harbor-800">
          A few specifics that come up often enough to name: deliberately
          misgendering someone or using a name they no longer go by counts.
          Publishing someone's private information without their permission
          counts. So does retaliating against a person for making a report.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold text-harbor-900 sm:text-3xl">
          What we expect from each other
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-harbor-800">
          Not harassing people is the floor. The room we're actually trying to
          build looks like this:
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-4 flex flex-col gap-3">
          <% [
               ["Be welcoming.", "Assume the person asking a basic question belongs here, because they do. Most of us were that person recently."],
               ["Be considerate.", "People come with different backgrounds, experience levels, jobs, and reasons for being in the room. Talk to them accordingly."],
               ["Be respectful in disagreement.", "Technical arguments are welcome. Contempt, condescension, and point-scoring are not."],
               ["Take responsibility.", "If you hurt someone, listen, apologize plainly, and correct it. Intent doesn't erase impact."],
               ["Look after the space.", "Follow the rules of whatever venue is hosting us, and leave it better than you found it."]
             ].each do |title, body| %>
            <li class="flex gap-3">
              <span class="mt-2 h-2 w-2 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-gold-400" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-harbor-800">
                <strong class="font-semibold text-harbor-900"><%= title %></strong>
                <%= body %>
              </p>
            </li>
          <% end %>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold text-harbor-900 sm:text-3xl">
          Where this applies, and what happens next
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-harbor-800">
          This covers our meetups, our online spaces, and any venue or
          after-event gathering where we are together as this group.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-harbor-800">
          Consequences are at the organizers' discretion, as the policy says.
          Depending on what happened that may be a private conversation, a
          warning, being asked to leave an event, or being barred from future
          ones. Organizers may act immediately to stop ongoing harm and sort out
          the details afterward.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-harbor-800">
          Organizers are held to this policy too. A report about an organizer
          goes to the other organizers, and that person takes no part in
          deciding it.
        </p>
      </section>

      <footer class="border-t border-marble-200 pt-6">
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-harbor-600">
          Suggestions and corrections are welcome —
          <%= link_to "open an issue", Site::GITHUB_URL, target: "_blank", rel: "noopener",
                class: "rounded-sm underline decoration-harbor-300 underline-offset-4 transition hover:text-harbor-900 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-harbor-500" %>.
        </p>
      </footer>
    </div>
  </div>
</article>
